Complete several personality profiles to understand how you can best use your natural wiring & gifts to lead a church planting team.

Description
Church planting is hard work. It requires a special person to be able to succeed. Several personality traits have been shown to be helpful to planters. The following list is adapted from a research project completed by Dr. Charles Ridely for 13 denominations on success factors for planters. (https://app.asana.com/app/asana/-/get_asset?asset_id=1202503599965553)
A good planter candidate:
    Can envision a desired future and sell the vision to others
    Is self-motivated
    Is able to create buy-in from others
    Is a successful evangelist
    Is a relationship builder
    Is more interested in health than quick growth
    Is an observer of the culture
    Is an equipper
    Is flexible and adaptable
    Is able to develop and empower teams
    Is resilient
    Has strong faith
Complete several personality profiles to determine if you have the leadership skills required to launch a church. These profiles can be used as a tool to confirm God’s calling.

Actions
    Instructions for Candidates to Access the CPCA assessment
    Click on the easy link: https://ministrygrid.lifeway.com/#/redeem-invite/MQLJ/RLWR
    Register for an account by providing First Name, Last Name, Email, and a Password.
    Click the “Purchase to Unlock” button on the Church Plant Candidate Assessment Course.
    Check out using our Lifeway Billing account information to unlock the course.
    Begin the CPCA course – chose whatever order of steps you prefer, but all 10 steps much be completed before your report will be generated.
    Have at least four 360 references returned before submitting “completed” on that step.
    Once the entire course is completed, email kevin@openbiblecentral.org and c.c. george@ram.network to notify them.


